WEBVTT

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.590
Aki, silent guardian with eyes of ice,

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:21.870
a question for you.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.100
What is an idol?

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.590
One with overwhelming power, 
who cannot be replaced.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.490
Haru, blazing deceiver wreathed in light,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.200
a question for you.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.520
What is an idol?

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.590
One who guides and commands the world.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.960
The object of worship for all things 
in creation. That is what we will be.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.810
No... what we must be.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.110
This is the vow we have made to the universe!

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.040
And if anyone...

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.860
...opposes us...

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.520
We'll destroy them.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:37.780
Love is a Mayfly

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:45.220
What is the greatest sin that man can commit?

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:48.180
Is it sloth?

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:49.640
Envy?

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.350
Wrath?

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.670
No.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.740
There is a sin that causes 
even more suffering.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:56.570
That sin is...

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.950
Beauty!

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.910
<b>Ouso Tsukuro</b>

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.960
Everyone runs in fear of my beauty!

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.370
Truly, beauty is the greatest sin!

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.950
That guy's such a creep.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.450
He says he has twenty TVs...

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.430
And that he's best friends 
with celebrities and stuff.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:19.650
Not even little kids try to pull 
those kinds of lies nowadays.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:24.070
This one time, I lost it and said "Oh, 
yeah? Then let's see your ten pet lions!"

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.350
and started walking to his house.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.450
What happened?

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.060
On the way there, he 
started writhing in pain.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.220
How come?

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:34.780
He said a long time ago, an alien placed 
a curse on his right hand and his heart,

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.190
and it had just started acting up.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.940
Oh, please. What a geek.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:42.140
I couldn't believe it. I started 
feeling kind of sorry for him.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.940
They're not lies!

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.700
So I just went home.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.160
They're not lies!

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:50.040
Why won't anyone believe me?!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:50.870
What the hell?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.120
In my mind, I can see the 4K TVs,

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:57.530
the lions, and the aliens clear as day!

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.560
Is it that they're too beguiled by my beauty?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.830
I confuse them so badly,

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.770
they refuse to believe the things I say?

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.440
Is it this sorrow that makes me beautiful?

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:17.230
That's it!

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.600
Beauty is sorrow.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.550
<i>Fool.</i>

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.090
<i>Beauty is strength.</i>

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.410
<i>Wrong.</i>

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.480
<i>Beauty is wit.</i>

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.310
Who's there?

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.860
Aliens?

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.230
My real mommy?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.210
Or some charming,

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.210
sexy devil come to kidnap me?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.220
Wrong and wrong, stupid.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:40.490
Although "devil" was closest, I suppose.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.870
You see, we want...

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.600
To corrupt you.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.350
That's why we're here.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:59.820
<b>1584th Pretty Boy Contest</b>

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.240
Already time for the pretty 
boy contest again, huh?

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.820
I wonder who'll win this time.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.570
You're so ignorant.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.460
To stand atop something so small

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.530
is a miniscule concern.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.550
I've met the people who stand

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.170
at the very top of the world!

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:18.130
One like the sun who makes my blood run hot,

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.960
and one like the moon who 
chills my soul to the core!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.320
Look, we've had enough.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.290
We're not falling for your lies again.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:27.690
It's not a lie!

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:31.010
I really met them!

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.960
Hey, watch where you're running.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:36.610
Can you stand?

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:38.850
You're...

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.910
Here through the exchange 
program. Beppu Haruhiko.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.870
And I am Akihiko.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.950
We're supposed to be joining 
the 2nd year class.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.790
Are our faces that weird to you?

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:53.580
Haru.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.120
You mustn't be so confrontational.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.930
I'm sure they've rarely seen our like before.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.150
They've never seen exchange students, either.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.130
Oh, I see.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.770
Anyway, pleased to meet you.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.940
No, it is <i>we</i> who are pleased!

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.580
Haruhiko-san! Akihiko-san!

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:11.050
See? You get it now?

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.720
I don't lie—

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.560
Beg your pardon! Press Society here!

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.670
Arriving like a bolt out of the blue,

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.690
Beppu Haruhiko-san and Akihiko-san.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.310
What are your hobbies?

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:24.720
Bonsai, gardening, and 
horseback riding, I suppose.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.510
Although I don't think I'll 
be able to do that here.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.920
I enjoy calligraphy.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:33.030
And I love to play Hungarian 
Pastoral Fantasy on the flute.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.570
Yes, yes, yes!

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:37.390
How celebrity and executive of you!

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:40.250
So, any intention to participate 
in the Pretty Boy Contest?

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:41.790
What's that?

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.940
We only just moved here,

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.590
so we're still getting our bearings.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.760
All questions must go through me!

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:51.720
And who are you, exactly?

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:55.810
I'm their number one worshipper and caretaker!

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:57.010
Isn't that nice?

00:06:57.010 --> 00:06:58.220
Interesting!

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.540
I can feel my biceps humming.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:05.270
I invite you to a duel of neurons!

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:07.870
I've been thinking...

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:08.660
What?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:09.740
<b>Earth Defense Club (lol)</b>

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:09.740
About what?

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:13.120
What are the conditions for 
being a main character?

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.890
You've lost me.

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:18.360
In the TV show known as life,

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:21.180
there's a clear difference between main 
characters and a side character, right?

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:22.080
True.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.540
So what separates a main 
character and a side character?

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:27.230
Good question.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.410
The kinds of people

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.320
who don't appear until 8 minutes 
and 30 seconds into the episode

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.870
can't be the main characters, right?

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.780
No, they can't.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:37.700
I think it's okay, as long as they 
get a lot to do in the second half.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.420
Oh, really?

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.640
Of course, I'm a side-character type,

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.120
so I don't know a lot about main characters.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:45.020
Oh, no.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:47.940
You're definitely a leading 
man, Kinugawa-senpai.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:48.940
Like tofu in broth.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.800
Does that count as a leading man?

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.130
I love tofu!

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:55.910
You can kill a man with it!

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.570
It's a deadly weapon?

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:00.620
But I suppose Atsushi can be frightening 
in the right circumstances.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.110
What are you talking about?

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:04.280
I'm hesitant in everything,

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.960
even when fighting as the Battle Lovers.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:09.380
The fact that you can say that without batting 
an eye just makes you more frightening.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.590
Actually, yeah.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:11.740
Good point.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:15.180
Please, please, please, please stop!

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:14.890
Speaking of which,

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.820
there's something I've been 
thinking about for a while.

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:19.640
Could that monster we fought 
be a leftover from last time?

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:21.810
No way.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:25.060
There's no way you've been thinking 
about that for a while, Yumoto.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.510
That's the part you're denying?

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.150
He probably just thought of it.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:29.610
Now, now.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.280
Let's hear him out.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.390
So?

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:35.180
The student council didn't send him out,

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.870
and Wom-san probably didn't, either.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.170
So what could it be?

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.950
W-Wait a moment!

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.790
What's all this "Wom-san <i>probably</i> didn't" stuff?!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.580
Don't you worry!

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:46.940
No matter what happens,

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:49.130
I believe you, Wom-san!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.600
You do not!

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.490
You clearly do not!

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:54.840
Well, we saw what you did to Mr. Tawarayama.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:57.770
The life I brought slipped out!

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.810
It was an accident! An accident, I swear!

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:02.520
What an incredible development!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:06.170
Are we about to see a 
no-holds-barred bloodbath?!

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:07.980
Boxing can hurt,

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.940
so we'll compete with feats of strength!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:10.610
<b>Grip Strength</b>

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:16.860
<b>Sidesteps</b>

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:19.830
<b>Pull-Ups</b>

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.570
I have to give you credit.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.540
You did have the guts to challenge me.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.170
Haruhiko-sama!

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.630
Next, battle of brains!

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.340
Could they be taking on 
the Millenium Problems?!

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.670
There wouldn't be anyone capable of judging it.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.050
<b>10 x 10 equation</b>

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:38.050
We'll do a 10 x 10 equation!

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.440
I'm done.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:41.260
Wh-What?!

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:43.580
Your time would be better spent studying

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:46.410
than challenging me, don't you think?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.520
Akihiko-sama!

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:53.680
The main/side character stuff reminded me.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:54.640
What?

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.420
Isn't it almost time for 
the Pretty Boy Contest?

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:59.660
Oh yeah, that's right.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.610
What? But you were so fired 
up about it before...

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:05.160
Yeah, but I've kind of stopped caring.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.370
I feel your thermal conductivity, Ryuu.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:09.330
Huh?

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.410
Hey, what's that supposed to mean?

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:14.340
Speaking of which. In front of my house...

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:17.720
Yumoto's defaulting to "speaking 
of which" a lot today.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:22.110
In the real world,
who actually says, "speaking of which"?

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:23.460
Same with "The aforementioned"

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:24.990
and "It just occurred to me"

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.770
or "Such-and-such"...

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.730
Just forget that and listen to me!

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.360
Fine, fine.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.950
So, what is it?

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:36.500
Shogi competition!

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.380
Check mate.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:41.530
Bow before me for eternity.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.070
Yes, forever!

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:44.120
Squee!

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:45.580
Cooking competition!

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.690
7.32 meters.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:51.040
My flavors might be poisonous for you.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.310
Since you'll never get it out of your mind.

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:54.670
Squee!

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.130
Sewing competition!

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:00.000
Take good care of this for me.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.120
And I'll take good care of you.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.260
Squee!

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:05.260
Fencing competition!

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:09.140
I've run your heart through.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:10.600
Squee!

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:13.570
More! Treat me with more contempt!

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.320
Look down your nose at me!

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:19.400
The eternal pretty boys of Binan High School,

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.270
Haruhiko-sama, Akihiko-sama.

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:23.860
We swear our eternal worship 
and submission to you!

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:24.570
We do!

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.920
What a burden.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.290
Don't be like that, Haru.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:31.980
Oh, no! Haru-sama, Aki-sama!

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:34.480
We don't intend to force ourselves on you!

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:36.630
We just really needed to...

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.610
I-I'm sorry!

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:44.340
We thought about our needs, 
but not about your feelings!

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.850
I feel like the king of the monkey pen.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:48.800
Truly, they are apes.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:54.860
<b>The Sparkling Prince
Battle Lover Scarlet
Finishing Move: Scarlet Love Lumiere
True Love Attack</b>

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:56.510
See?

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:58.010
It's there, like I said!

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.770
When did they put up a building like this?

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:01.740
It looks like a castle.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.100
Looks like a love hotel.

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:06.720
Nah, love hotels are cheaper than that.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.370
This thing's at least two million yen per square meter.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:11.080
How do you know that?

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.330
Instinct?

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:15.510
I do have my real estate 
broker license, you know.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:17.540
Do you think it's a house?

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.760
If it's not a love hotel, it must be.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:25.260
I could have done without hearing 
Atsushi say "love hotel."

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.260
Same here.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.470
I agree.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:28.810
Why?!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.140
What's a love hotel?

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.880
What is this feeling? Motherly instinct?

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.640
The smell of innocence.

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:38.780
It's so soothing!

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.840
Never change, Yumoto.

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.670
Yes, remain ignorant!

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:45.070
Hey! What was that?!

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:45.070
A true heir to the throne of love!

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.200
Darn it!

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.370
Oh, are you customers?

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.830
Come on in! The bath's open right now!

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.370
Did you hear that? "Customers," he says.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:00.050
Let it go, Haru. That's the class 
of person we're dealing with.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:04.130
We've moved into the house across the way.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:06.470
Oh, really?

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:10.060
We were saying, it looks like 
a love hotel! Just amazi—

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.290
We apologize on his behalf.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:16.020
He just meant that it was very impressive.

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:19.540
We won't forget your face, Hakone Yumoto.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.040
I'm sure we'll be speaking again, very soon.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.490
We hope you'll be accommodating.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.030
Yeah, sure thing!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:25.740
Oh, that's right!

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.320
<b>Bath Coupon
Kurotama Bath</b>

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:30.150
Here, these are coupons for our bath!

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:31.990
Please use them!

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.430
I'm <i>horribly</i> grateful.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.170
We'll treasure them.

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:49.010
Hey... Haruhiko-sama? Akihiko-sama?

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:51.720
I'm very grateful to you for inviting me...

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.570
But being the only one here...

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:56.430
I'm just delighted... awe-struck, really...

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:01.150
<i>Ladies... of which there are none.</i>

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.190
<i>Gentlemen!</i>

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.250
<i>Welcome to the VEPP Theater.</i>

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:07.590
Huh? Did he say Beppu Theater?

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:11.710
<i>I'm proud to introduce that marvelous duo...</i>

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:14.080
<i>The VEPPer!</i>

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:16.040
English? Vapor?

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.940
<i>Now's the time!</i>

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:19.720
<i>Enjoy the show!</i>

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:30.800
<i>VEPPer, the twin stars 
racing through the galaxy!</i>

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.060
<i>Let's illuminate the mysteries 
of the universe...</i>

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:37.180
<i>On the name of the stars!</i>

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:50.600
<i>VEPPer, the twin stars 
racing through the galaxy!</i>

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:54.280
<i>Let's illuminate the mysteries 
of the universe...</i>

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.890
The twin stars shining in the heaven!

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:55.910
Salty Sol!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:57.830
Melty Luna!

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:02.170
Galaxy Idols, the VEPPer!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.590
Chosen warrior!

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.550
Lucky you!

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.510
Happy you!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.840
Shooting...

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.720
Star!

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:22.780
We have new neighbors across 
from the bath, then?

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.480
I wonder if they'll use our coupons!

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:27.440
I'm sure they will.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:28.530
Yeah!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.160
By the way, big bro...

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:35.620
What's a love hotel?

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:41.500
You don't know, either?

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:42.330
I'm sorry.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.750
Why are you apologizing?

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:04.630
My name is Tofu Monster!

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:07.180
I possess the delicate mind

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:09.820
and silky white beauty of tofu!

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:16.160
It's time to Love Making 
into the Battle Lovers!

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:18.520
We left our curry back there...

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:19.870
What a waste.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:22.500
I had to cut off a great texting session!

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.870
I was just thinking about the London markets.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.820
Get to the Love Making already!

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:29.090
Let's finish it up quick!

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.700
Love Making!

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.300
The Sparkling Prince!

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.600
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:42.230
The Flashing Prince!

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:44.440
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:46.970
The Piercing Prince!

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:49.280
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.400
The Roaring Prince!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.600
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:56.950
The Thrilling Prince!

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.140
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:03.540
This love-filled planet will 
not abide those who lack love!

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:07.250
Those who wield loveless 
power must kneel before love!

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:08.950
Love is power!

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:10.460
Love is hope!

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:12.150
Be born for love!

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:13.920
Give your life for love!

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.090
Love!

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:18.080
We are, forever, the heirs 
to the throne of love...

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.390
Battle Lovers!

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:21.140
Feel the power...

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.270
Of love!

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:27.600
I don't care if you're tofu or atsu-age!

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:31.110
I want to know why you're 
here, and who sent you!

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:35.320
If you want to know, you'll 
have to beat me first!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.070
Domestically-Grown GMO-Free Soybean Shot!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.330
Tofu is made from soybeans, you know!

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:48.960
Obviously!

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.540
But don't you think you're better than just soybeans?

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.940
Tofu doesn't judge!

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:54.920
Soy Curd Storm!

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:01.930
I can't stand curd! It's so gross and mushy!

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:03.520
Be consumed by the dilemma

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.890
of having to eat fragile 
food with chopsticks!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.980
It's sticking in my throat!

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:11.690
I don't think I like this monster.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.190
Is there any monster you <i>do</i> like?!

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:18.650
The curds...

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:20.070
They're so slick...

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.980
This guy's stronger than I thought!

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.540
What should we do?

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:38.880
Stop wasting food!

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:42.800
Scarlet Love Lumiere!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.010
Chilled tofu?!

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:51.810
At least soybean isoflavone 
is a great moisturizer...

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.340
Y-You can't beat me!

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:57.030
I'm delicate and beautiful!

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:59.200
Don't avert your eyes from the truth!

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.410
Even if you are tofu, right now,

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.490
you're the tofu dregs left behind in the pot!

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.770
But whether you get recycled 
for rice porridge the next day

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:07.790
is up to you!

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:16.250
True Love Attack!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:29.400
True Love Fountain!

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:41.780
Love is over!

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:45.730
Hey, he's from C class...

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:47.290
Oh, I remember him.

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.020
Someone definitely made him a monster, then.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:54.650
Speaking of which, we forgot to 
ask about the monsters' boss!

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:57.710
That's a proper use of "speaking 
of which," at least.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.320
Senpai!

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.740
What's that there?

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:12.650
Five of them, and not a 
decent-looking one in the bunch.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:14.150
Just trash from start to finish.

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:15.800
Really?

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:18.720
I suppose there might be one 
or two eccentrics out there

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:21.110
who they might appeal to.

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.820
What was that, you guys?!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:26.050
If they're blurring their faces like that...

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:30.290
They must be using advanced 
technology like ours.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.730
And they seem to be naturally rude.

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.500
Not pleasant at all.

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:39.300
I see no reason to be 
considerate of your feelings.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.260
We're inconsiderately

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:43.990
going to be wiping you out soon, after all.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.800
The hell do you mean "wiping us out"?

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:49.520
We, the VEPPer,

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:53.060
cannot allow your continued existence.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:55.020
Understand, loser nerds?

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:58.230
Are you trying to pick a fight with us?

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.220
Did you finally catch on?

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:04.610
You're awfully slow on the 
uptake. It worries me.

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:13.190
That's enough for today.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:16.040
We don't want you catching 
their nerd lameness.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:18.260
You're so right, Dadacha.

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:22.080
Well, you're not going to have 
a comfortable night from now on.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:24.470
Keep that in mind, loser nerds.

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:26.380
Wait, you...

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:31.980
Just who were those guys?

00:21:39.050 --> 00:21:40.200
What's all this?

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:42.980
You're horribly in our way, apes.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.350
Come on, you're making trouble.

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:46.420
Make way.

00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:53.270
Chopping wood?

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.640
That must be hard work.

00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:56.710
Oh, thank you.

00:21:57.780 --> 00:21:58.960
Excuse us.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:11.660
What was that all about?

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:21.880
We, the Beppu Apes

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:24.660
stand ready to serve you. 
Haru-sama, Aki-sama.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:27.250
Your wish is our command.

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:05.790
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:05.790
Brotherly Love

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:04.020
Next time, "Brotherly Love."

00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:05.380
Love Making!
